WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:05.680
Well, I finally received the results of my
coronavirus test, and they were negative.

00:00:05.840 --> 00:00:07.120
Yes! That’s a relief!

00:00:07.120 --> 00:00:10.020
Hooray, now we can finally isolate as a family!

00:00:13.160 --> 00:00:18.019
We’re very fortunate that we can keep doing
this show from our private office, but a lot

00:00:18.019 --> 00:00:19.460
of people aren’t so lucky.

00:00:19.460 --> 00:00:24.679
As the coronavirus forces many businesses
to shut down, people everywhere are losing

00:00:24.679 --> 00:00:28.460
their jobs or seeing their hours dramatically
scaled back.

00:00:28.460 --> 00:00:34.870
As of March 21st, 3.3 million Americans filed
for unemployment, the largest number in history

00:00:34.870 --> 00:00:36.320
by a wide margin.

00:00:36.320 --> 00:00:40.970
The previous record was set in 1982 at 695,000.

00:00:40.970 --> 00:00:43.830
And this might just be the beginning.

00:00:43.830 --> 00:00:49.150
Some economists predict that by this summer,
over 14 million Americans will have lost their

00:00:49.150 --> 00:00:50.150
jobs.

00:00:50.150 --> 00:00:51.920
It’s a unique situation.

00:00:51.920 --> 00:00:57.330
In past unemployment crises, the government
usually tries to encourage businesses to increase

00:00:57.330 --> 00:01:02.970
hiring, but this time, we actually want people
to stay home to slow the spread of disease.

00:01:02.970 --> 00:01:08.200
So Congress recently passed a $2 trillion
dollar stimulus package that includes a massive

00:01:08.200 --> 00:01:13.270
expansion of unemployment insurance to help
keep Americans afloat while we wait out the

00:01:13.270 --> 00:01:14.270
storm.

00:01:14.270 --> 00:01:18.650
Even if you still have your job, this bill
will most likely affect you, so you should

00:01:18.650 --> 00:01:19.780
know what’s in it.

00:01:19.780 --> 00:01:21.270
First… free money!

00:01:21.270 --> 00:01:26.170
If you are a United States resident with a
social security number, not claimed as a dependent,

00:01:26.170 --> 00:01:32.310
and made less than $75,000 last year, you
will receive a $1,200 check from Uncle Sam,

00:01:32.310 --> 00:01:35.889
plus $500 for each child you have under 16.

00:01:35.889 --> 00:01:40.759
The more you made over $75,000, the smaller
the check gets and is totally phased out for

00:01:40.759 --> 00:01:43.359
people with incomes greater than $99,000.

00:01:43.359 --> 00:01:49.170
But, married filers earning less than $150,000
together get the full amount.

00:01:49.170 --> 00:01:57.359
So if Dan makes $105K and Marsha makes $40K,
they still both get $1200 each, plus $1500

00:01:57.359 --> 00:01:58.520
for their three kids.

00:01:58.520 --> 00:02:02.099
You do not have to apply or sign up or do
anything at all to get that money.

00:02:02.099 --> 00:02:06.990
It’s a one time payment based on your 2019
gross income, and should be arriving in about

00:02:06.990 --> 00:02:11.890
3 weeks or so by mail or direct deposit, if
you already have that set up with the IRS.

00:02:11.890 --> 00:02:17.500
If you haven’t filed your 2019 taxes yet,
they can use your gross income from your 2018

00:02:17.500 --> 00:02:18.690
tax return…

00:02:18.690 --> 00:02:23.320
But if you still haven’t filed that either,
you should ASAP, or risk not getting your

00:02:23.320 --> 00:02:24.320
check.

00:02:24.320 --> 00:02:29.530
And if you happened to make over $100,000
in 2019 but expect to lose that income this

00:02:29.530 --> 00:02:30.530
year…

00:02:30.530 --> 00:02:33.280
well, unfortunately you won’t qualify.

00:02:33.280 --> 00:02:34.280
Sorry.

00:02:34.280 --> 00:02:38.380
Next, the bill provides a dramatic increase
in unemployment insurance.

00:02:38.380 --> 00:02:44.250
Traditionally, unemployment insurance is only
available to people who lose full-time W2

00:02:44.250 --> 00:02:46.470
jobs through no fault of their own.

00:02:46.470 --> 00:02:52.040
It usually lasts about 26 weeks, and pays
around 45% of lost wages.

00:02:52.040 --> 00:02:55.360
But this bill expands pretty much all of that.

00:02:55.360 --> 00:03:00.630
Freelancers, part-timers, gig-economy workers,
and even people who still have jobs but had

00:03:00.630 --> 00:03:04.840
their hours cut can all now apply for unemployment
insurance.

00:03:04.840 --> 00:03:09.890
You’re also eligible if you were about to
start a new job, or are too new to a job to

00:03:09.890 --> 00:03:11.710
normally qualify for benefits.

00:03:11.710 --> 00:03:16.420
If the closure of a school or nursing home
means you have to quit your job and stay home

00:03:16.420 --> 00:03:20.090
to take care of someone, you are eligible
for unemployment insurance.

00:03:20.090 --> 00:03:25.160
Basically, if the coronavirus pandemic has
severely hampered your ability to make money,

00:03:25.160 --> 00:03:28.210
you probably qualify for some kind of benefit.

00:03:28.210 --> 00:03:32.710
How much and for how long depends on your
state and your previous income level, but

00:03:32.710 --> 00:03:38.011
the federal government is increasing the duration
across the board by 13 weeks, and the benefit

00:03:38.011 --> 00:03:40.630
amount by $600 a week.

00:03:40.630 --> 00:03:45.390
Here in Texas, weekly unemployment benefits
are calculated by taking your highest-earning

00:03:45.390 --> 00:03:50.750
quarter of the last year and dividing by 25,
up to a maximum of $454.

00:03:50.750 --> 00:03:57.590
So Timothy, who was making about $30K a year
waiting tables before his restaurant shuttered,

00:03:57.590 --> 00:04:01.640
would normally be eligible for $300 a week
for 26 weeks.

00:04:01.640 --> 00:04:08.000
Now, thanks to this bill, he’ll be getting
$900 a week and his benefits will last for

00:04:08.000 --> 00:04:09.000
39 weeks.

00:04:09.000 --> 00:04:12.600
You might be thinking… wait, that’s more
than he was making before!

00:04:12.600 --> 00:04:15.180
And while that’s true, there is a catch.

00:04:15.180 --> 00:04:20.630
That extra $600 a week is only available for
four months, ending July 31st.

00:04:20.630 --> 00:04:26.100
So unless Congress extends it, he’s only
getting $900 for the first 16 weeks.

00:04:26.100 --> 00:04:31.030
Since most experts doubt that either this
medical or financial crisis will be over by

00:04:31.030 --> 00:04:33.970
then, Timothy is hardly on easy street.

00:04:33.970 --> 00:04:37.940
This bill isn’t a magic wand that will keep
us all afloat in perpetuity.

00:04:37.940 --> 00:04:43.690
It’s a temporary life raft to buy Americans
some time, and a way to keep money flowing

00:04:43.690 --> 00:04:45.639
through the economy in the short term.

00:04:45.639 --> 00:04:51.280
There’s a lot more in it we haven’t discussed:
student loan suspensions, funds for healthcare,

00:04:51.280 --> 00:04:57.340
an expansion of loans available to small businesses,
and of course, a $500 billion loan package

00:04:57.340 --> 00:05:00.010
for large businesses and municipalities.

00:05:00.010 --> 00:05:04.940
We’ll be talking about those things in the
weeks to come, but for now, if your income

00:05:04.940 --> 00:05:10.220
has been impacted by the coronavirus pandemic,
grab yourself a seat on Uncle Sam’s life

00:05:10.220 --> 00:05:12.190
raft while there’s still room.

00:05:12.190 --> 00:05:17.350
It will give you the breathing space to take
a fresh look at your finances and plan for

00:05:17.350 --> 00:05:19.190
what comes next.

00:05:19.190 --> 00:05:20.040
And that’s our two cents!

